.TH PROJECT-EON 6 "August 2026" "Project Eon" "Games"
.SH NAME
project-eon \- preservation-first Millennium 2.2 and Deuteros launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B project-eon
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B project-eon
starts Project Eon, an SDL3 reimplementation project for Millennium 2.2 and
Deuteros.  It does not include or unpack game data.  Original media is supplied
by the user, hash-verified, and read in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line usage and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-data " path"
Use a user-supplied directory or archive as the read-only data source.
.TP
.BI \-\-game " millennium|deuteros"
Select a game after its exact original release has been verified.
.TP
.B \-\-inspect
Report recognised, user-supplied media without launching a game.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.projecteon
Default user-supplied data location on Linux.  Looking it up does not create it.
.SH COPYRIGHT
